{"id":"u-8c245d58-bdc0-4ce7-a804-d804aaca95d7","src":"community","title":"Zodd Protocol","author":"Tristan  H.","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/gDTFLA-mess-around","desc":"Schedule: Either 1 on, 2 off (preferred), or Monday, Thursday, Saturday, repeat (If needed)\nMain Lift Progression: Top set (RPE 9.5-10), Backoff set (RPE 7-8.5) for weeks 1-3, 3x10 (RPE 7-9) week 4, on weeks 5-8 either add weight, reps, or improve form\nIntensity matter more than arbitrary rep count: If you go above the rep count on weeks 1-4, add 2.5% to the weight on weeks 5-8 for each rep extra (I have low intensity on Jeffersons and Bulgarians, but you may do an intensity appropriate to you)\nExample: Week 3: 5 reps 90% RPE 10; therefore, on week 7 do 95%\nSecondary Lift Progression: Start on bottom of RPE range on weeks 1 & 5. Top set: Do weight until at bottom of RPE range, then add weight, repeat. Backoff set: Do weight until top of rep range & Bottom of RPE range, then add weight, repeat.\nIsolation Progression: Triple progression: Add reps, then add weight, reset when form gets sloppy. You can do this for individual sets, you do not have to wait on both sets to cap out before adding weight to one.\nMain lift Warmup: 2 x 10 empty bar, 1 x 8 40%, , 1 x 5 60%, 1 x 2 75%, Hold 90% for 10s/1 x 85% for deadlifts, rest as needed, should not need to be too long. (2m after last warmup is a good base line)\nSecondary Lift warmup: Weeks 1-4: 1 x 5 empty bar, 1 x 5 65% of working weight, 1 minute rest. Weeks 5-8: 1 x 5 empty bar, 1 x 8 50% of working weight, 1 x 2 80% of working weight, rest as needed\nIsolation warmup: 1x8 60% of working weight, 1x1 100% of working weight, rest as needed\nMain Lift Rest Times: Squats & Deadlifts (3m 30s), Bench, Pull up, & Bent Over Row (3m)\nSecondary Lift Rest Times: Bulgarian Split Squats (1m 30s each leg), Jefferson Curl & Belt Squat (3m), Upper body lifts (2m 30s), Dips (3m)\nIsolation Rest Times: Leg superset (1m 15s between lifts), Upper body super sets (1m between lifts), shorten-biased isolations (2m), Lengthened biased isolations (2m 30s)\nExercise Swapping: Any muscle hit a 3rd time in the plan using an isolation can be swapped for an isolation of a different muscle. All isolations can be switched for a preferred one as long as it is close enough\nExample: Ez Bar Preacher curl -> Barbell preacher curl or Machine Preacher curl is a good swap, but Ez Bar Preacher Curl - > Spider Curl is not\nVolume Adjustments: Run the whole program twice, have your sleep, diet, and intensity dialed in, and if then you still do not see results, add volume where you need it.\nCardio Day 1: 5m backwards bike before lift, 10m jog after lift\nCardio Day 2: 10m moderate pace Rows\nCardio day 3: 5m backwards bike before lift, After lift (Bike): 1m slow, 40s slow, 20s sprint, done twice, 30s slow, 30s sprint, done twice, 1m slow.","level":["Intermediate","Advanced"],"goals":["Muscle","Strength"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":90,"joins":0,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-10-05T15:05:10.298Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Heavy","Light","Medium"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"ss":[{"n":"Leg Extension","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":10,"rpe":10},{"lo":10,"hi":15,"rpe":10}],"rest":60},{"n":"Nordic Curl","sets":[{"amrap":1,"rpe":10,"x":2}],"rest":60}]},{"n":"Squat (Low Bar)","sets":[{"r":8,"pct":80},{"r":10,"pct":68}],"rest":210},{"n":"AD Press","sets":[{"r":8,"pct":80},{"r":10,"pct":68}],"rest":180},{"n":"Overhead Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"amrap":1,"pct":78}],"rest":180},{"n":"Hip Thrust (Machine)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":8,"rpe":8},{"lo":10,"hi":12,"rpe":9}],"rest":180},{"n":"Reverse-Grip Bench Press (Smith)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":8,"rpe":8},{"lo":10,"hi":12,"rpe":9}],"rest":150},{"n":"Lat Pulldown (Close Grip)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":8,"rpe":8},{"lo":10,"hi":12,"rpe":9}],"rest":150},{"n":"Hanging Leg Raise","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":10,"rpe":9},{"lo":6,"hi":10,"rpe":10},{"lo":10,"hi":15,"rpe":10}],"rest":120},{"n":"Hip Adductor (Machine)","sets